# Repository Knowledge Map

This map explains the project-owned paths and routes Agents to durable authority. It describes documents and directories, not a command system. After setup handoff, the target remains independently useful through its Markdown, Plans, runbooks, Git history, project commands, and host-native Agents.

## Reading protocol

1. Read root [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md).
2. For substantive work, inspect [`exec-plans/active/`](exec-plans/active/) and resume or create exactly one matching ordinary Markdown Plan.
3. Follow that Plan's exact reads, boundaries, acceptance criteria, and current checkpoint.
4. Read only the relevant authority and use project-owned commands from [`QUALITY.md`](QUALITY.md) or [`OPERATIONS.md`](OPERATIONS.md).

Completed Plans, superseded documents, and accepted decisions are durable records, not general startup context. Package absence after setup is expected and is not `UNKNOWN`, blocking, or a residual risk for ordinary target work.

